meta {
  name: Search Vectors
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/vector/search
  body: json
  auth: basic
}

auth:basic {
  username: {{admin_username}}
  password: {{admin_password}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "query": "experience et technologies backend de Maxime Jolivet",
    "collection_name": "cv_maxime_jolivet",
    "limit": 5
  }
}

docs {
  Custom controller, not an ApiResource -- snake_case fields (collection_name,
  category_id, document_type, language, complexity), plain application/json.
  The intelligent-analysis filters (document_type/language/complexity) only
  match documents that went through DocumentAnalysisService -- check a
  chunk's metadata (List Messages / this response) for the actual values
  indexed for your documents before filtering on them. All filters present
  combine with AND. Every successful call here is logged as a SearchQuery
  row (visible only in /admin/search-queries, no API for it).

  CAVEAT (verified against this collection): any payload filter
  here (language/complexity/document_type/category_id) makes QdrantClient
  bubble up a 500 wrapping Qdrant's own 400 for the "cv_maxime_jolivet"
  collection -- Qdrant Cloud's `strict_mode` is enabled on it with no
  payload indexes created, and strict_mode rejects filtered queries against
  unindexed payload fields. Unfiltered search (as in the body above) works
  fine. This is a Qdrant Cloud collection configuration issue, not an
  App\VectorConnector bug -- create a payload index for a field
  (`PUT /collections/{name}/index`) directly against Qdrant before relying
  on filters against this particular collection.
}
